2026-08-25T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2059) 'A status report carries three parts in order:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2059) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2059) '1. The bottom line comes first. The opening sentence states the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2059) '   outcome plainly, the slip, the failure, the result, with no
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2059) '   buffer, no apology, and no warm-up. A reader who reads only this
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2059) '   line knows where the work stands.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2059) '2. The explanation follows. It gives the factual reason for the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2059) '   outcome; the reader already holds the result, so the explanation
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2059) '   carries the why without holding it back.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2059) '3. The next step closes the report: the fix underway, the alternative
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2059) '   open to the reader, or the time of the next update.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2059) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

